Automatically Load and Unload Parts at a Sensor
Load and Unload Parts at the Sensor of a Conveyor
In our example we will demonstrate how to place parts from a processing station onto a Conveyor with the
PickAndPlace robot. A second PickAndPlace robot then loads the parts onto pallets on a second Conveyor.
The pallets, which the Conveyor transports, are then unloaded with the third PickAndPlace robot onto
another processing station. The Drain finally removes the parts from the plant.
We show how to configure the PickAndPlace robot and the Conveyors:
• With drag-and-drop. Here the PickAndPlace robot automatically creates the required sensors and
controls and enters the corresponding angle into the Angles Table.
Automatically Load and Unload Parts at a Sensor
Plant Simulation Help 10-667
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Manually on the tab Exit in the list Target Selection. Here you have to create the required sensors and
program the controls yourself.
In our example we will:
• Configure the Material Flow Objects
• Configure the Robots
The finished simulation model looks like this:
Back to Pick and Place Parts with the PickAndPlace Robot
Configure the Material Flow Objects
The Source named SourceParts produces parts and moves them to the Station named Station1. The
PickAndPlace robot named PlacePartOnConveyor picks the part up, rotates to the Conveyor and places
it onto the Conveyor. To model this, drag the PickAndPlace robot onto the Conveyor and select the
Configure the Material Flow Objects
10-668 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Operation > Place part. Plant Simulation then automatically creates the respective sensor on the
Conveyor.
The Conveyor transports the placed part over a certain distance. A second Source named SourcePallets
produces pallets for a second Conveyor. The PickAndPlace robot named LoadPallets loads the parts from
the Conveyor onto the pallets. To model this, drag the PickAndPlace robot onto the Conveyor and select
the Operation > Load part. Plant Simulation then automatically creates the respective sensor on the
Conveyor.
The PickAndPlace robot named UnloadPallets unloads the parts from the pallets onto the Station2. To
model this, drag the PickAndPlace robot onto the Conveyor and select the Operation > Unload part.
Plant Simulation creates the corresponding control for unloading the pallet at the respective sensor. The
corresponding exit behavior here is Exit strategy or target control. The fully processed parts are then
moved from Station2 to the Drain named PartsOut which removes them from the plant.
Insert the required objects so that they match the figure below:
